om/difference-between-esp32-vs-raspberry-pi/","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"04a5e2fd2610d22a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDifference between ESP32 vs Raspberry Pi The differences between ESP32 vs Raspberry Pi are discussed below. What is the ESP32 Development Board? The ESP32 is a small, powerful, and low-cost microcontroller with integrated Bluetooth, WiFi & AI capabilities, so it is used in IoT and home Automation projects.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"04a5e2fd2610d22a\">>>","siteName":"www.elprocus.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8f04f8873c63eb97\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nESP32 vs. Raspberry Pi: Which One Should You Choose?\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8f04f8873c63eb97\">>>","url":"https://eduengteam.com/esp32-vs-raspberry-pi-which-one-should-you-choose/","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d6d6bb4522c91786\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nESP32 vs . Raspberry Pi : Which One Should You Choose? - Educational Engineering Team In the ever-evolving landscape of DIY electronics, two platforms stand out as favorites among makers: the ESP32 and the Raspberry Pi . Both have captured the imagination of hobbyists and students alike, each offering unique features and capabilities. Whether you're a seasoned engineer or just starting your ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d6d6bb4522c91786\">>>","siteName":"eduengteam.com"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1776923740418}}
{"type":"message","id":"6402cd59","parentId":"1b362965","timestamp":"2026-04-23T05:55:54.737Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ESP32 is generally better suited for IoT projects due to its low power consumption and real-time performance. However, Raspberry Pi has more processing power and can handle more complex tasks.\n\nThe ESP32 Development Board is a small, powerful, and low-cost microcontroller with integrated Bluetooth, WiFi & AI capabilities, making it ideal for IoT and home Automation projects.\n\nFor beginners, the ESP32 may be easier to use due to its simpler programming environment. However, Raspberry Pi offers more flexibility and can handle more complex tasks, making it a better choice for experienced developers.\n\nUltimately, the choice between ESP32 and Raspberry Pi depends on your specific project requirements and needs."}],"stopReason":"stop","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"llama3.1","usage":{"input":9821,"output":131,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9952,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1776923754735}}
