{"type":"message","id":"d549a2f5","parentId":"640f6d03","timestamp":"2026-04-23T06:36:54.495Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"To search for and install a local shell or command execution skill on ClawHub, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the ClawHub website at https://clawhub.ai/\n2. Use the search bar to find skills related to shell or command execution.\n3. Once you've found the desired skill, click on it to view its details.\n4. Click the \"Install\" button to install the skill in your local environment.\n\nAlternatively, you can use the ClawHub CLI to search and install skills from the command line.\n\nIt's also worth noting that you can find more information about using ClawHub to manage skills in OpenClaw on various online resources, such as the OpenClaw documentation or online tutorials."}],"stopReason":"stop","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"llama3.1","usage":{"input":15554,"output":146,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15700,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1776926214487}}
